<title>FRANCE: Thomson-CSF opens lower at 158 Ffr/shr.</title>
<headline>Thomson-CSF opens lower at 158 Ffr/shr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in French defence electronics firm Thomson-CSF opened lower on Thursday at 158 francs per share, compared to a Tuesday close of 161.20.</p>
<p>The shares resumed trading today after being suspended on Wednesday pending news of the privatisation of its parent Thomson SA.</p>
<p>The government yesterday said it preferred Lagardere Groupe's bid for Thomson over a rival offer from Alcatel Alsthom and was referring both bids to the Privatisation Commission.</p>
</text>
